WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:03.701
-It doesn't get much cooler
than Eric Idle.

00:00:03.701 --> 00:00:06.467
Yes. No, you. Exactly. Yes.
-Oh, okay. Fine. I'm cold.

00:00:06.467 --> 00:00:08.100
-No.
-I'm so cool, I'm cold.

00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:10.400
-You are so cool, you're cold.
Oh, my gosh.

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:12.300
We got to talk
a little bit backstage.

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:14.033
First of all, thank you
for coming back on the show.

00:00:14.033 --> 00:00:17.400
You know you're one of my
favorite humans of all time.

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:19.067
You're one of my favorite
comedians of all time.

00:00:19.067 --> 00:00:20.868
I love you.
I absolutely love you.

00:00:20.868 --> 00:00:23.133
-Oh, well, thank you very much.
Thank you very much..

00:00:23.133 --> 00:00:24.167
-It means a lot
that you're here.

00:00:24.167 --> 00:00:25.701
-I don't think comedians
are humans,

00:00:25.701 --> 00:00:28.334
but, I mean, you know,
I appreciate what you're saying.

00:00:28.334 --> 00:00:29.868
-But you were telling me
that you learned a lot

00:00:29.868 --> 00:00:31.467
about your ancestry.

00:00:31.467 --> 00:00:33.267
-Yes.
I've been studying my ancestry.

00:00:33.267 --> 00:00:35.133
And I did that thing
called ancestry.com.

00:00:35.133 --> 00:00:36.467
-Yeah.

00:00:36.467 --> 00:00:38.701
-And it was very interesting,
because I found out --

00:00:38.701 --> 00:00:46.667
I didn't know and I found out
that I was 39,942,003rd in line

00:00:46.667 --> 00:00:48.567
to the British throne.

00:00:48.567 --> 00:00:50.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:50.667 --> 00:00:56.667
So if something happens
to 39,931,000, accident --

00:00:56.667 --> 00:00:57.801
you know,
accidents can happen.

00:00:57.801 --> 00:00:58.968
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
It's interesting.

00:00:58.968 --> 00:01:01.200
-I will be king.
-Oh, my gosh!

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:04.100
Basically, we have
royalty on the show.

00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:06.033
-Exactly.
-Oh, I'm so excited.

00:01:06.033 --> 00:01:07.968
Well, who knows? Yeah.

00:01:07.968 --> 00:01:09.934
I want to talk to you
about Spamalot, though.

00:01:09.934 --> 00:01:11.968
Congratulations.
It is back on Broadway.

00:01:11.968 --> 00:01:14.200
This is a big deal.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:16.968
The original
Broadway production,

00:01:16.968 --> 00:01:19.634
this won three Tonys,
including Best Musical.

00:01:19.634 --> 00:01:21.100
-Best Musical, yeah.

00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:24.234
-And it is one of the
funniest plays I've ever seen.

00:01:24.234 --> 00:01:26.400
But before "Spamalot,"
weirdly enough --

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:27.868
I did a little research here

00:01:27.868 --> 00:01:31.400
and found out you were
once nominated for a Tony?

00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:33.567
-Yes, a long time ago,
I used to --

00:01:33.567 --> 00:01:35.000
I lived in England, in London,

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:37.667
and I got an envelope
in the mail one day.

00:01:37.667 --> 00:01:39.434
And I opened it.
A big, beautiful envelope.

00:01:39.434 --> 00:01:41.501
And it said, "Congratulations!

00:01:41.501 --> 00:01:46.701
You have been nominated
for Best Actress on Broadway."

00:01:46.701 --> 00:01:50.100
And I'd never been to Broadway
or even America.

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:53.100
But so I wrote back and said,
"This is very moving for me.

00:01:53.100 --> 00:01:56.968
I'm very honored, because, 'A,'
I've not been on Broadway,

00:01:56.968 --> 00:01:59.868
and 'B,'
I'm not really an actress.

00:01:59.868 --> 00:02:03.033
I have worn women's clothing
on television from time to time,

00:02:03.033 --> 00:02:04.300
but not really an actress."

00:02:04.300 --> 00:02:07.133
And, so, I accepted,
and then I never heard any more.

00:02:07.133 --> 00:02:11.100
And it turned out
it was for Chita Rivera.

00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:12.434
-What?!

00:02:12.434 --> 00:02:16.000
-Well, how do you send it to
London to Chita Rivera?

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:18.667
You know?
Anyway, so, I was that close

00:02:18.667 --> 00:02:21.234
to being in the remake
of "West Side Story."

00:02:21.234 --> 00:02:23.334
-Oh, that's not true.
That's not -- Okay.

00:02:23.334 --> 00:02:25.434
Come on.
-Yeah.

00:02:25.434 --> 00:02:27.534
-"Spamalot"
is based on the movie

00:02:27.534 --> 00:02:28.767
"Monty Python
and the Holy Grail."

00:02:28.767 --> 00:02:29.868
-It is.

00:02:29.868 --> 00:02:32.501
-And it's
very, very, very funny.

00:02:32.501 --> 00:02:35.334
You actually put it up
in Washington recently,

00:02:35.334 --> 00:02:37.968
at the Kennedy Center,
and it just destroyed.

00:02:37.968 --> 00:02:39.133
It crushed.

00:02:39.133 --> 00:02:41.000
-The Washington critic said,
"It's not fair

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:44.334
to make me laugh this much,"
which I like that as a review.

00:02:44.334 --> 00:02:46.133
That's quite nice, isn't it?
-Yeah, that is a great --

00:02:46.133 --> 00:02:47.701
So, is that the reason why
you're bringing it

00:02:47.701 --> 00:02:49.033
back to Broadway?

00:02:49.033 --> 00:02:50.334
-They wanted to bring it.

00:02:50.334 --> 00:02:51.834
It's a Kennedy Center
production.

00:02:51.834 --> 00:02:54.133
And we put some more people
in from "SNL"

00:02:54.133 --> 00:02:55.634
and very good casting people.

00:02:55.634 --> 00:02:58.200
And, yeah, I'm looking for--
I haven't actually seen it,

00:02:58.200 --> 00:03:00.100
so I'm going to go
and see it soon, shortly.

00:03:00.100 --> 00:03:03.033
-Yeah, the voice of God --

00:03:03.033 --> 00:03:05.200
-Yes. No, we've had
a problem with that,

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:07.167
because the voice of God
is there,

00:03:07.167 --> 00:03:09.067
and last time
we were on Broadway,

00:03:09.067 --> 00:03:11.167
John Cleese played God.

00:03:11.167 --> 00:03:12.601
You know, obviously.
[ Applause ]

00:03:12.601 --> 00:03:15.868
And now -- But, you know,
now, you know,

00:03:15.868 --> 00:03:17.334
he's getting on a bit.

00:03:17.334 --> 00:03:18.701
He's getting up there.

00:03:18.701 --> 00:03:22.300
And, also, you know, I mean,
John's gone a bit strange,

00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:23.601
you know.

00:03:23.601 --> 00:03:25.868
I mean, remember he threw
water over me on your show?

00:03:25.868 --> 00:03:26.968
-Yeah, we got in trouble.
-Right here.

00:03:26.968 --> 00:03:28.868
And you don't want God
who throws water

00:03:28.868 --> 00:03:30.467
over people, you know, do you?

00:03:30.467 --> 00:03:32.467
I mean, Moses says,
"Hello, God,"

00:03:32.467 --> 00:03:34.334
and he throws
a bucket of water over him?

00:03:34.334 --> 00:03:35.400
-Yeah, you don't want that.

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:37.200
-Apart from now
he's a burning bush.

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:38.667
You know, they're going
to put him out.

00:03:38.667 --> 00:03:42.000
So we fired him.
-Yes. Fired John Cleese.

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:44.033
-And I played him
for a little while.

00:03:44.033 --> 00:03:48.067
I was playing God,
and then I fired myself

00:03:48.067 --> 00:03:49.234
because I wasn't very good.

00:03:49.234 --> 00:03:50.367
-Yeah, what'd that feel like?

00:03:50.367 --> 00:03:51.501
-Well, it was quite good,
actually.

00:03:51.501 --> 00:03:53.467
I quite enjoyed firing myself.
-Yeah.

00:03:53.467 --> 00:03:55.501
Are you still in a good
relationship with yourself?

00:03:55.501 --> 00:03:57.467
-Eh, I'm not
talking to me, really?

00:03:57.467 --> 00:03:59.601
But apart from that...

00:03:59.601 --> 00:04:01.767
-I wouldn't talk to you
either -- if I were you.

00:04:01.767 --> 00:04:04.434
-So, anyway,
we found somebody else,

00:04:04.434 --> 00:04:08.300
and I can announce it tonight
because he said I can.

00:04:08.300 --> 00:04:12.334
And God is going to be
played by Steve Martin.

00:04:12.334 --> 00:04:14.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:16.334 --> 00:04:18.033
-That's fantastic.

00:04:20.234 --> 00:04:21.701
God will be played
by Steve Martin.

00:04:21.701 --> 00:04:24.601
And then I want you to come back
on after you fire him.

00:04:24.601 --> 00:04:26.501
-Okay.

00:04:26.501 --> 00:04:29.133
-I'm so excited you're here.
Everyone go see "Spamalot."

00:04:29.133 --> 00:04:33.267
Eric Idle, everyone.
"Spamalot" is back on Broadway.

00:04:33.267 --> 00:04:37.400
Go see Steve Martin as God
at the St. James Theatre.

00:04:37.400 --> 00:04:39.934
Rick Ross and Meek Mill
perform for us after the break.

00:04:39.934 --> 00:04:41.133
Stick around, everybody.

